@lang en
IMPORT `pvi-health-assessment`

-- Tests of PART I (PHẦN I: NGUYÊN TẮC CHUNG). Every expected value is a figure the source prints
-- (15 days, 60, 65, 18, 1 year, 130%, 50%, 30 days, 80%, 100%, one year) applied by hand to a
-- scenario; both sides of every threshold are asserted. Calendar facts used: 1 January 2026 is a
-- Thursday; 1 July to 31 December 2026 is 184 days counting both ends; 2026 has 365 days.

§ `Tests — Part I`

§§ `Age (clause 2.1, "tính theo lần sinh nhật gần nhất")`

#ASSERT `age at the last birthday` (YMD 2000 3 10) `on` (YMD 2026 3 9)  EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `age at the last birthday` (YMD 2000 3 10) `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `age in days` (YMD 2026 1 1) `on` (YMD 2026 1 16) EQUALS 15

§§ `Clause 1 — geographic scope`

#ASSERT `clause 1 — the geographic scope of` `personal accident` EQUALS `the whole world`
#ASSERT `clause 1 — the geographic scope of` `inpatient treatment` EQUALS `Vietnam`
#ASSERT `clause 1 — a place is within the geographic scope of` `personal accident` `, the place being in Vietnam:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 1 — a place is within the geographic scope of` `outpatient treatment` `, the place being in Vietnam:` FALSE)

§§ `Clause 2.1 — age and residence`

-- From 15 days old: 14 days is too young, 15 days is accepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` FALSE))
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 16) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` FALSE)
-- To 60: aged 60 is accepted; aged 61 only if continuously insured since 60.
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 1965 6 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 1964 6 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` FALSE))
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 1964 6 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` TRUE)
-- To 65: aged 65 continuously insured is accepted; aged 66 is not.
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 1960 6 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — of an age PVI accepts on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, for` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 1959 6 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` TRUE))

`a foreign visitor` MEANS `An insured person` WITH
    `date of birth`                              IS YMD 1990 5 15
    `a woman`                                    IS FALSE
    `residence status`                           IS `neither a Vietnamese citizen nor a foreigner residing in Vietnam`
    `health status when the insurance was taken out` IS `a healthy status`
    `continuously insured with PVI since age 60` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — a Vietnamese citizen or a foreigner residing in Vietnam` `a foreign visitor`)
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — a Vietnamese citizen or a foreigner residing in Vietnam` `the adult woman`

§§ `Clause 2.1 — children`

-- Under 18: on a parent's contract, for no more than the lower parent's sum insured.
-- The child's sum insured in these fixtures is 200,000,000.
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — a person under 18 is insured with a parent, for no more than the parent` `the child of seven` (`a certificate for` `2026, every rider` `after` EMPTY `, schedule` `the schedule` `, programme` 1 `, waiting periods shown:` TRUE `, with a parent:` TRUE `, parents' sums insured` (LIST 300_000_000, 200_000_000) `, terminated early on` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — a person under 18 is insured with a parent, for no more than the parent` `the child of seven` (`a certificate for` `2026, every rider` `after` EMPTY `, schedule` `the schedule` `, programme` 1 `, waiting periods shown:` TRUE `, with a parent:` TRUE `, parents' sums insured` (LIST 300_000_000, 150_000_000) `, terminated early on` NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — a person under 18 is insured with a parent, for no more than the parent` `the child of seven` (`a certificate for` `2026, every rider` `after` EMPTY `, schedule` `the schedule` `, programme` 1 `, waiting periods shown:` TRUE `, with a parent:` FALSE `, parents' sums insured` EMPTY `, terminated early on` NOTHING))
-- 18 is not "under 18".
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — a person under 18 is insured with a parent, for no more than the parent` (`a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 2008 1 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` FALSE) `the first-year certificate`

-- From 15 days to under 1 year: programme 1 or 2 only.
`the infant` MEANS `a healthy citizen born on` (YMD 2025 8 1) `, a woman:` FALSE `, continuously insured since 60:` FALSE
#ASSERT     `clause 2.1 — a person under 1 year is on programme 1 or 2` `the infant` `the child's first-year certificate`
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.1 — a person under 1 year is on programme 1 or 2` `the infant` (`a certificate for` `2026, every rider` `after` EMPTY `, schedule` `the schedule` `, programme` 3 `, waiting periods shown:` TRUE `, with a parent:` TRUE `, parents' sums insured` (LIST 300_000_000) `, terminated early on` NOTHING))

-- 130% of the 51-60 premium for ages 61-65; 130% of the 1-3 premium under 1 year.
#ASSERT `clause 2.1 — the premium for an insured person aged 61 to 65, given` 10_000_000 EQUALS 13_000_000
#ASSERT `clause 2.1 — the premium for an insured person under 1, given` 4_000_000 EQUALS 5_200_000

§§ `Clause 2.2 — persons PVI does not accept`

GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A health status`
`a status with a disability rate of` `the rate` MEANS `A health status` WITH
    `suffering from a mental illness`            IS FALSE
    `suffering from leprosy`                     IS FALSE
    `suffering from cancer`                      IS FALSE
    `rate of disability or permanent injury`     IS `the rate`
    `under treatment for an illness or injury`   IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.2 — PVI does not accept a person whose health status is` (`a status with a disability rate of` (49%)))
#ASSERT     `clause 2.2 — PVI does not accept a person whose health status is` (`a status with a disability rate of` (50%))
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 2.2 — PVI does not accept a person whose health status is` `a healthy status`)
#ASSERT     `clause 2.2 — PVI does not accept a person whose health status is` (`A health status` WITH `suffering from a mental illness` IS FALSE, `suffering from leprosy` IS FALSE, `suffering from cancer` IS TRUE, `rate of disability or permanent injury` IS 0, `under treatment for an illness or injury` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT     `clause 2.2 — PVI does not accept a person whose health status is` (`A health status` WITH `suffering from a mental illness` IS FALSE, `suffering from leprosy` IS FALSE, `suffering from cancer` IS FALSE, `rate of disability or permanent injury` IS 0, `under treatment for an illness or injury` IS TRUE)

#ASSERT     `clause 2 — the person is eligible to be insured under the certificate` `the adult woman` `the first-year certificate`

§§ `Clause 3 — other insurance`

#ASSERT `clause 3 — the costs left for PVI after another contract paid` 6_000_000 `, of` 10_000_000 EQUALS 4_000_000
#ASSERT `clause 3 — the costs left for PVI after another contract paid` 12_000_000 `, of` 10_000_000 EQUALS 0

§§ `Clause 4 — the premium`

#ASSERT     `clause 4 — PVI is not liable because the premium was not paid in full and on time` `the renewed certificate, premium unpaid`
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 4 — PVI is not liable because the premium was not paid in full and on time` `the renewed certificate`)

§§ `Clause 5.2 — early termination`

GIVEN `by` IS A `A party`
      `written` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given` IS A DATE
      `effective` IS A DATE
      `for non-payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `claim paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A notice of early termination`
`a notice by` `by` `, written` `written` `, given` `given` `, effective` `effective` `, for non-payment` `for non-payment` `, claim paid` `claim paid` `, paid in full` `paid in full` MEANS
    `A notice of early termination` WITH
        `given by`                               IS `by`
        `in writing`                             IS `written`
        `date given`                             IS `given`
        `date of termination`                    IS `effective`
        `because the insured person breached the duty to pay the premium` IS `for non-payment`
        `a claim has been paid in the certificate's term` IS `claim paid`
        `premium paid in full`                   IS `paid in full`

-- At least 30 days: 30 days' written notice is valid, 29 is not, an oral notice is not.
#ASSERT     `clause 5.2 — the notice of early termination is valid` (`a notice by` `the insured person` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 5.2 — the notice of early termination is valid` (`a notice by` `the insured person` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 5 30) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 5.2 — the notice of early termination is valid` (`a notice by` `the insured person` `, written` FALSE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE))

-- The insured person may not postpone the date notified.
#ASSERT `clause 5.2 — the termination date that takes effect, when the notice is` (`a notice by` `the insured person` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE) `and the insured person asks to postpone it to` (YMD 2026 8 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 1

-- The remaining period from 1 July 2026 to 31 December 2026: 184 days; its premium, pro rata to a
-- premium of 3,650,000 over 365 days: 1,840,000.
#ASSERT `clause 5.2 — the days remaining after early termination on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, under` `the first-year certificate` EQUALS 184
#ASSERT `clause 5.2 — the premium for the remaining period after termination on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, under` `the first-year certificate` EQUALS 1_840_000
-- The insured person ends it, no claim paid: 80% of 1,840,000 = 1,472,000; with a claim paid: none.
#ASSERT `clause 5.2 — the premium refunded on early termination` (`a notice by` `the insured person` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE) `the first-year certificate` EQUALS 1_472_000
#ASSERT `clause 5.2 — the premium refunded on early termination` (`a notice by` `the insured person` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE) `the first-year certificate` EQUALS 0
-- PVI ends it, not for non-payment, the premium paid in full: 100% = 1,840,000.
#ASSERT `clause 5.2 — the premium refunded on early termination` (`a notice by` `PVI` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, for non-payment` FALSE `, claim paid` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE) `the first-year certificate` EQUALS 1_840_000
-- PVI ends it for non-payment: left to the law in force, declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `clause 5.2 — the premium refunded on early termination` (`a notice by` `PVI` `, written` TRUE `, given` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, effective` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, for non-payment` TRUE `, claim paid` FALSE `, paid in full` FALSE) `the first-year certificate`

§§ `Clauses 5.3, 9, 11 — PVI's permissions`

-- Unconditional: PVI may refuse to renew, may examine, may refuse a dishonest claim. Each is a
-- permission, so not acting is no breach.
#TRACE `clause 5.3 — PVI may refuse to renew at the end of the term` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `PVI` DOES `refuse to renew` AT 0
#TRACE `clause 9 — PVI may have the insured person medically examined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `PVI` DOES `have the insured person medically examined` AT 3
#ASSERT `clause 9 — who bears the cost of the medical examination` EQUALS `PVI`
#ASSERT `clause 11 — the premium refunded after cancellation for dishonesty` EQUALS 0

§§ `Clauses 6, 7, 8 — changes, the term, the law`

#ASSERT     `clause 6 — a change of benefits can take effect on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` `the first-year certificate`
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 6 — a change of benefits can take effect on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, under` `the first-year certificate`)
#ASSERT     `clause 7 — the term is one year` `2026, every rider`
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 7 — the term is one year` (`a period from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, all riders:` TRUE `, no higher:` TRUE `, premium paid:` TRUE))
#ASSERT `clause 8 — the governing law` EQUALS "the law of Vietnam"

§§ `Clause 10 — PVI's liability`

#ASSERT `clause 10 — the last day of PVI's liability under` `the renewed certificate` EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `clause 10 — the last day of PVI's liability under` `the renewed certificate terminated on 1 July 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 30
#ASSERT     `clause 10 — a day within PVI's liability under` `the renewed certificate terminated on 1 July 2026` `:` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 10 — a day within PVI's liability under` `the renewed certificate terminated on 1 July 2026` `:` (YMD 2026 7 1))
#ASSERT     `clause 10 — a day within PVI's liability under` `the renewed certificate` `:` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 10 — a day within PVI's liability under` `the renewed certificate` `:` (YMD 2027 1 1))
